Today's entry is **Tinder for middle children**. The startup is **Also**, a dating app where every match has to type your name correctly before the chat unlocks. Metadata generation and `validate-entry.sh` both passed after the final edits.

- **Roll:** took 1 reroll, because the first draw (GitLab for introverts) was already in history. "Middle children" was used once before in `starbucks-for-middle-children`, but this company/subject pair is new.
- **Design:** a flat "label-maker" style: buttercup yellow background (#FBF0C9), blue label tape (#1F3FA8), tomato red (#E4482B), with Fredoka, Nunito, IBM Plex Mono and Permanent Marker fonts. It doesn't match any of the last 7 entries.
- **Images:** used all 4. Three are profile photos for the demo's swipe cards and one is Dana Okafor's testimonial headshot. All passed the vision check on the first try. I skipped a hero image because the style is typographic, and the hero phone mockup reuses the first card photo.
- **Landing page:** hero, three features, three testimonials and three pricing tiers. The middle tier, "Middle Seat", is labelled "Most overlooked".
- **Demo:** a swipeable card stack with birth-order filters and a "hand-me-down queue". Tapping "Notice" opens a pop-up where you type their name. Three wrong tries reassigns them to your brother.
- **Gallery:** `site/index.html` was rebuilt and now shows 132 entries. The only changes are the new slide and the count.
- **History and log:** `state/history.json` has the new entry appended, and the run summary is in `state/runs/2026-10-23.log`.

**Problems hit:**
- The validator's first run failed because it read an image path built in the demo's JavaScript as a missing file. I changed how the demo sets the image source and validation passed.
- The screenshot check found the crossed-out sibling names in the hero overlapping the headline. I moved them beside the word "name", added a mobile layout, and the re-capture showed it fixed.

The screenshots were saved to `docs/design-catalogue/`, which is gitignored. I ran no git commands.

